    <article class="prose about-copy">
      <p>By day I run international content operations at <b>KukuFM</b>, where I own the localisation engine behind our expansion into Southeast Asia: dubbing Hindi microdramas into Bahasa Indonesia, building the acquisition slate, and running the performance and influencer marketing that gets them watched. Before that I set up KukuFM&rsquo;s Movies category and ran the marketing for its first film.</p>
      <p>I&rsquo;m drawn to the small operational decisions that quietly become strategy: who gets context, where quality is defined, what a team measures, and which exceptions are allowed to stay exceptional. That is what most of this writing is about.</p>
      <p><em>Margin of Error</em> is where I work those questions out in public. I write about AI without pretending the implementation is incidental, about marketing beyond the campaign, and about media as both culture and machinery.</p>
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>I trained as an engineer at IIT (BHU) before MICA and my way into product, marketing, and media, which is probably why I trust a spreadsheet and distrust it in equal measure. This site is intentionally not a r&eacute;sum&eacute;. The writing is the longer introduction.</p>
